Start Hermes sessions on the always-on Hermes host instead of a sandbox each.

A session with the hermes agent only forwards its turns to the user's own
Hermes over SSH, so a sandbox gives it nothing but a start of several seconds.
The deployment runs one Omnigent host for these sessions in an always-on Pod,
and POST /v1/sessions starts a Hermes session that would get a sandbox on that
host instead, whichever client creates it. omnigent_hermes_host (ours, in
images/server/) decides: only with OMNIGENT_HERMES_HOST_ID set, only for a
top-level session whose harness is hermes-remote, and only while the host is
online and the caller's; otherwise the session gets its sandbox as before. A
create that names the host for another agent is refused, an automation
without a pinned host never picks it, and GET /v1/hosts marks it hermes_only
so the web UI's host pickers leave it out
(web-patches/0040-hide-hermes-host.patch).
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0023-cors-origins.patch.
